  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mahesh Ahuja vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 4 May, 2023 Author: Anand Pathak Bench: Anand Pathak 1 In The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh At Gwalior Crr No. 1894 of 2023 (Mahesh Ahuja Vs The State Of Madhya Prades Dated : 04-05-2023",
    "facts": "The petitioner has been convicted under Sections 7 (i), r/w 16 (1) (a) (i) and 7 (ii) r/w 16 (1) (a) (i) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954 and under Section 7 (v) r/w rule 44J & 16 (1) (a) (i) of Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954 and Prevention of Food Adulteration Rule, 1955 and sentenced to undergo RI for 6-6 months with fine of Rs.2000-2000/-, with default stipulations.",
    "arguments": "It is the submission of the learned counsel for the petitioner that he is the owner of a general store and he has no role to play regarding packaging and mixture of tobacco items as alleged against him.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "It is the submission of the learned counsel for the petitioner that he is the owner of a general store and he has no role to play regarding packaging and mixture of tobacco items as alleged against him.",
